I found a workaround. It uses reflection but that's acceptable as a one-time operation during app start.

```cs
public abstract class Animal { }

public class Dog : Animal { }
public class Cat : Animal { }
```

```cs
// one-time reflection
var names =
  Assembly.GetExecutingAssembly()
  .GetTypes()
  .Where(x => x.IsAssignableTo(typeof(Animal)))
  .Where(x => x != typeof(Animal))
  .Select(x => x.FullName!);
Func<LogEvent, bool> matcher = logEvent => 
  names.Select(name => Matching.FromSource(name))
  .Any(predicate => predicate(logEvent));

// config
.WriteTo.Logger(x => x
  .Filter.ByExcluding(matcher)      // or .Filter.ByIncludingOnly(matcher)
  .WriteTo.Console()
)
```

I'm closing as this is good enough for my use case.

Both options (the built-in formatter and Expressions) only parse the template once, at start-up, so parsing speed is not a big difference between them. Expressions adds a small overhead, but this is mostly because of theming support.

A very simplistic benchmark (ignoring the added `StringWriter` allocation overhead) to compare them:

```
BenchmarkDotNet v0.14.0, macOS Sequoia 15.1.1 (24B91) [Darwin 24.1.0]
Apple M3 Pro, 1 CPU, 11 logical and 11 physical cores
.NET SDK 9.0.100
  [Host]     : .NET 9.0.0 (9.0.24.52809), Arm64 RyuJIT AdvSIMD
  DefaultJob : .NET 9.0.0 (9.0.24.52809), Arm64 RyuJIT AdvSIMD
```

| Method            | Mean     | Error   | StdDev  | Ratio |
|------------------ |---------:|--------:|--------:|------:|
| FormatBuiltin     | 121.8 ns | 0.61 ns | 0.57 ns |  1.00 |
| FormatExpressions | 136.2 ns | 0.28 ns | 0.25 ns |  1.12 |

Low tens of nanoseconds per event is negligible in normal usage.

Here's the source, so you can drop it into a .NET 8 console app and try whatever formats are important in your scenario:

```cs
using BenchmarkDotNet.Attributes;
using BenchmarkDotNet.Running;
using Serilog.Events;
using Serilog.Formatting;
using Serilog.Formatting.Display;
using Serilog.Parsing;
using Serilog.Templates;

BenchmarkRunner.Run<FormattingBenchmark>();

public class FormattingBenchmark
{
    readonly ITextFormatter _expr = new ExpressionTemplate("[{@t:HH:mm:ss} {@l:u3}] {@m}\n{@x}");

    readonly ITextFormatter _builtin =
        new MessageTemplateTextFormatter("[{Timestamp:HH:mm:ss} {Level:u3}] {Message:lj}\n{Exception}");

    readonly LogEvent _evt = new(
        DateTimeOffset.Now,
        LogEventLevel.Information,
        exception: null,
        new MessageTemplateParser().Parse("Hello, {Name}!"),
        [new LogEventProperty("Name", new ScalarValue("nblumhardt"))]
    );
    
    public FormattingBenchmark()
    {
        var e = FormatExpressions().ToString();
        var b = FormatBuiltin().ToString();
        if (!e.Contains("INF")) throw new InvalidOperationException("?");
        if (e != b) throw new InvalidOperationException("=");
    }
    
    [Benchmark(Baseline = true)]
    public StringWriter FormatBuiltin()
    {
        var sw = new StringWriter();
        _builtin.Format(_evt, sw);
        return sw;
    }
    
    [Benchmark]
    public StringWriter FormatExpressions()
    {
        var sw = new StringWriter();
        _expr.Format(_evt, sw);
        return sw;
    }
}
```

