@otto-gebb in your case, you can use `Prefix_` instead, and rename fields for ElasticSearch only, if you want to keep your logs compatible with the rest of the Serilog ecosystem. 

The trick is:

1. Use a consistent prefix for names you want indexed:

```csharp
Log.Information("Hello, {Prefix_Name}", name);
```

2. Write an enricher that renames those fields

```csharp
class PrefixRenameEnricher : ILogEventEnricher
{
    public void Enrich(LogEvent evt, ILogEventPropertyFactory pf)
    {
        var prefixed = evt.Properties.Where(p => p.Name.StartsWith("Prefix_")).ToList();
        foreach (var p in prefixed)
        {
            evt.RemovePropertyIfPresent(p.Name);
            evt.AddOrUpdateProperty(new LogEventProperty(p.Name.Replace("Prefix_", "prefix."), p.Value));
        }
    }
}
```

3. Attach it to a sub-logger for ElasticSearch only

```csharp
Log.Logger = new LoggerConfiguration()
    .WriteTo.Console() // Regular sink
    .WriteTo.Logger(lc => lc
       .Enrich.With(new PrefixRenameEnricher())
       .WriteTo.Elasticsearch(...))
    .CreateLogger();
```

