@tebeco I think you may have misunderstood the OP; the question is about the style used in the example code, not what the library supports.

Serilog was designed from the start to be usable without any static state. Just configure your IoC container to inject the right `ILogger` into the right components and you're done! The log4net global `LogManager`/category name system works in some cases, but in others (e.g. multitenancy) you need independent logging pipelines _even for the same caller_.

`Log.Logger` is the simplest path for most people, but Serilog absolutely does account for non-static logging pipelines, you might need to dig around a bit more to work out how to support your precise scenario, though. Shoot some questions to the Gitter if you need a hand.

