Hi! Thanks a million for providing the executable repro, much appreciated.

This is an expected behavior change introduced as [a bug-fix in 2.7](#1165). The problem with your configuration is that the enrichment (i.e. from `LogContext`) is being configured to run asynchronously:

```csharp
private static void WithConfig(WebHostBuilderContext ctx, LoggerConfiguration config)
{
    var serilogfile = ".\\tormentor-[TODAY].txt";
    config.WriteTo.Async(a =>
    {
        a.File(serilogfile.Replace("[TODAY]", DateTime.Now.Date.ToString("yyyy-MM-dd")),
                outputTemplate:
                "{Timestamp:HH:mm:ss} [{Level}] [Test: {TEST}] [Test 2: {TEST2}] CorrelationId: {CorrelationId} Message: {Message}{NewLine}{Properties}{NewLine}{Exception}")
            .Enrich.FromLogContext()
            .MinimumLevel.Override("Microsoft", LogEventLevel.Warning)
            .MinimumLevel.Override("System", LogEventLevel.Warning);
    });
}
```

This would mean that, by the time the enricher runs (on a background thread) and looks at `LogContext`, it's probably already been `Pop()`'d.

This won't do anything at all in 2.7 with `Async()`, since although it's tricky to tell from the API, `Async()` only works for sinks. To keep the same style of config, you could use `Async(wt => wt.Logger(...))`, but that won't work quite as you expect either, because of the minimum level configuration being applied at the wrong point.

What you really want is:

```csharp
private static void WithConfig(WebHostBuilderContext ctx, LoggerConfiguration config)
{
    var serilogfile = ".\\tormentor-[TODAY].txt";
    config
        .Enrich.FromLogContext()
        .MinimumLevel.Override("Microsoft", LogEventLevel.Warning)
        .MinimumLevel.Override("System", LogEventLevel.Warning)
        .WriteTo.Async(a =>
            a.File(serilogfile.Replace("[TODAY]", DateTime.Now.Date.ToString("yyyy-MM-dd")),
                    outputTemplate:
                    "{Timestamp:HH:mm:ss} [{Level}] [Test: {TEST}] [Test 2: {TEST2}] CorrelationId: {CorrelationId} Message: {Message}{NewLine}{Properties}{NewLine}{Exception}"));
}
```

HTH!
