I think that rather than call `MessageTemplate.Render()`, you're going to need to iterate through the template tokens and output each one.

You can strip the `"` from string values by a few methods, the easiest is probably just to detect string properties and write them out directly (my guess is that because of your other requirements, you'll also be checking `pt.PropertyName` to make some choices during this loop):

```csharp
foreach (var token in logEvent.MessageTemplate.Tokens)
{
    var pt = token as PropertyToken;
    if (pt == null)
    {
        token.Render(logEvent.Properties, output, null);
        continue;
    }

    LogEventPropertyValue propertyValue;
    if (!logEvent.Properties.TryGetValue(pt.PropertyName, out propertyValue) ||
        ((propertyValue as ScalarValue)?.Value as string) == null)
    {
        token.Render(logEvent.Properties, output, null);
        continue;
    }

    output.Write(((ScalarValue)propertyValue).Value);
}
```

