It's a _tiny bit_ hacky (okay, quite a bit ;-)) but you could combine a destructuring policy and an enricher to do this.

1. The destructuring policy - adds a `AsString` property to the result:

```csharp
.Destructure.ByTransforming<Voltage>(v => new { v.Value, v.Unit, AsString = v.ToString() })
```

2. The enricher looks for structures with a `AsString` property and flattens them out:

```csharp
class AsStringEnricher : ILogEventEnricher
{
    public void Enrich(LogEvent logEvent, ILogEventPropertyFactory propertyFactory)
    {
        foreach (var p in logEvent.Properties)
        {
            var sv = p.Value as StructureValue;
            if (sv != null)
            {
                var s = sv.Properties.SingleOrDefault(sp => sp.Name == "AsString");
                if (s != null)
                {
                    logEvent.AddOrUpdateProperty(new LogEventProperty(p.Key, s.Value));
                    foreach (var sp in sv.Properties)
                    {
                        if (sp != s)
                            logEvent.AddOrUpdateProperty(sp);
                    }
                    break; // Don't enumerate after modifying ;-)
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```

