Aha :+1: your code should read:

``` csharp
var programLogger = loggingService.ForContext<Program>();
programLogger.Information("## Starting Web Job ##");
// etc.
```

The result of `ForContext<T>()` is a logger instance that you need to call through in order to record the context.

To do the ambient context instead you can add `Enrich.FromLogContext()` to your `LoggerConfiguration` and write:

``` csharp
using (LogContext.PushProperty(Constants.SourceContextPropertyName, typeof(Program).FullName))
{
    loggingService.Information("## Starting Web Job ##");
    // etc.
```

(`LogContext` is more often used for pushing properties like `MessageId` and so-on, hence the lack of a type-based push method.)

