@DmitryNaumov - the `File()` sink syncs writes by default; in 2.0 a `buffered` parameter was added to override this: https://github.com/serilog/serilog-sinks-file/blob/dev/src/Serilog.Sinks.File/FileLoggerConfigurationExtensions.cs#L59 - buffered writes are normally an order of magnitude (or two) better than sync'd ones, worth checking out if you can afford to sacrifice some durability.

`PeriodicBatchingSink` is in: https://github.com/serilog/serilog-sinks-periodicbatching in case that helps.

